2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,7897,11/02/2023,2. General Maint - High Priority,wiring on arm are exposed.,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/10/2023 06:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 11/10/23  4:54:15 AM: Ordered new dispenser/foam control motor assembly. Got all swapped out. Fixed some bolts while doing this. Sprayed the dispenser ball screw with lithium grease. Worked in and out manually and it is moving much easier. Missy said they were getting a motor overheating error. I think this was connected but will monitor. Adjusted recipe as needed and machine is running good now.,[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,10514,02/26/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Foam Machine lost power,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/12/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/12/24  9:49:59 AM: Checked fuse inside the back electrical box. It was blow. Replaced with new and turned machine on. Everything turns on good. Got mold setup in machine and running. Adjusted after we came back from lunch. It ran all the way through lunch with no issues, just needed more foam. Got adjusted where it is making a good mold. Machine is good to go. | Preston Ellexson - 02/26/24  7:32:26 AM: We have power going into the machine, but nothing on the machine side. I locked this out. After a job in process, I will inspect the machine for the issue.",[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,11503,05/03/2024,6. General Maint,foam machine not working,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/09/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/09/24 10:08:11 AM: Got the bearings and board in. Put the jaw assembly completely back together. Re-installed on the machine. Put on the new FE board. Started machine and mold. Made recipe adjustments but was still having issues. Got the code from Ronnie and adjusted the film speed, film reverse distance, and door power. Fine tuned the recipe just before lunch. Went back over after, and it was still running good. | Preston Ellexson - 05/06/24  7:44:55 AM: There are 2 bearings that need replaced on this. It is non operational. The film doesn't roll right due to this issue and back feeds up into the machine. I had to rob a board from this 5/3 to get the small trimline IMold running. I ordered bearings and a board overnight and they should be here today. I already removed the jaw assembly from the machine. I have it disassembled and cleaned in maintenance. When parts arrive, I'll just have to put the jaw assembly back together, put it on the machine, and install the board.",[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,12322,07/10/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Paint cell foam machine cut wire open,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/11/2024 09:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 07/11/24  7:46:40 AM: Inspected machine for any obvious issues. Nothing appears to be wrong. Unplugged boards and restarted machine with same result. I just rebuilt a complete jaw assembly and had it in maintenance. I took off the cross cut seal assembly and put on this machine. No more errors. Adjusted the recipe quite a bit. Machine is running good with good molds. Getting another cross cut seal assembly ordered today.,[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,12847,08/22/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Control on left table busted,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/23/2024 01:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/23/24 12:27:11 PM: Replaced lift table hand control with new. On a new one, they send the cable and all. Kept new cable and just replaced the control. Existing cable was in good shape with no bare spots or wiring. Adjusted the left film sensor. It was throwing an error for the film path because this sensor wasn't adjusted at the accurate range. Got done and ran a handful with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24 12:32:38 PM: I have the key for this machine. Everything is still running good just the lift table is locked out. I will try and knock this out tomorrow.",[]
