2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,13838,11/15/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Foam machine in 3049 cell Door did reach closed position,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/19/2024 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 11/25/24  7:10:19 AM: Swapped door assembly out with a used one. Adjusted the recipe as needed. Got with Ronnie for the code to make more adjustments. Adjusted the film reverse distance and checked all other extra settings. Machine is running good now.,[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,14032,12/10/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door won't close screen goes blank  foam machine in 3049,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston/Derek,Maintenance,0,12/10/2024 09:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 12/11/24  4:23:26 AM: Checked the machine. Door pressure was low. Got it adjusted and checked everything else. Made small adjustments to the recipe. Started machine and let it warm up and run. Didn't have any issues with the first 20. Made a few more adjustments on the recipe and machine is running good.,[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,16516,07/28/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Machine still saying error. Eject did not reach pressure.,Closed and Completed,0,8,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/29/2025 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/29/25  8:21:00 AM: I've been working on this off an on for 2 weeks. They originally kept getting a calendar motor error. Sometimes it would continue to happen, and sometimes they could get it running. Since this has been a hinderance for a week or so now, I went ahead and swapped out the entire jaw assembly with a rebuilt one from maintenance. Spent time getting the recipe adjusted and running good. Everything is running good as of 7/15. Johnny has called me a few times week of 7/21 for the pressure issue. I normally just remove the tank line and let it bleed out. Then I go into the settings and calibrate the eject. This typically fixes the machine and will continue running. 7/28 I worked on this. Swapped out the bloffer due to the other foam pad being loose and moving. Cleaned all teflon and cut wire. Recipe is good. Tried running machine and the compressor is making too much noise in comparison to normal. Swapped the compressor out with a new one. Got covers put back on and lines ran. Turned machine on and started with no issues. After it warmed up everything is working really good.",[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,16978,09/11/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,paint cell foam machine has a hole leaking air from the tank,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/16/2025 09:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 09/17/25  4:06:54 AM: Had tank in maintenance that I had already welded up. Removed the one from the machine. Removed top and bottom air fittings and put on repaired tank. Got all swapped out and everything put back on the machine. Turned on and calibrated eject. No issues with air or leaking. Got machine running. No adjustments needed to recipe. Made over 30 pcs with no issues. Machine is running good.,[]
2143,EQ ID 2143,Vendor Foam Machine,Assembly,17140,10/06/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,paint cell foam machine. says mold box not clear seems to be the eye sensors.,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/06/2025 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 10/06/25  8:00:00 AM: Tested the sensor. It is still working but needed the sensitivity adjusted. Got it set and mounted the sensor back on tight. Started machine and it's working good. Didn't have to make any adjustments to the recipe. Molds look good once warmed up.,[]
2145,EQ ID 2145,Big Ass Fan,Assembly,3073,10/28/2022,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,Big Ass Fan above Large Cell is wobbling as if unstable.  Need maintenance to checkfor bearing issue.,Closed and Completed,0,3,Josh/Preston,Maintenance,0,03/18/2023 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 03/23/23  4:16:36 AM: Fan blades were removed. All bolts were inspected and tightened. Guy wires were checked. All is good so fan blades were put on. We tested starting from 10% to 100% and the fan looks good. We see no issues at all throughout any speed. | Joshua Patton - 03/15/23  4:38:39 AM: I will look at this on 03/18/23,[]
