2087,EQ ID 2087,PMU 1 Work Order,Assembly,15064,03/14/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",2 Rivet gun,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/14/2025 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/18/25  4:14:17 AM: Got the battery chargers from PMU. They also had a brand new battery. Got batteries charging while I inspected rivet guns. On one the nosepiece for angle head extension was loose. Removed needed parts and found it was partially stripped out. Got a file and cleaned the threads. Put all back together and spray lubed the head assembly. Gun is pulling rivets good now. Sent back to PMU with a fresh battery. Took apart the other gun and found the internal piston rod was almost completely unthreaded. Got everything tightened back up and put together. Tried a rivet and the battery goes dead within a pull or two of the trigger. After charging, it appears we have 2 bad batteries that won't hold a charge. Got another good battery charged and running. Sent back to PMU with the chargers and bad batteries. Let Johnny know.",[]
