234,EQ ID 234,Stand-Up Forklift #2,Assembly,12780,08/15/2024,6. General Maint,wheel has a chunk missing causing a wobble.,Closed Without Action,0,1,Preston/Medley,Maintenance,0,08/21/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/21/24 11:49:02 AM: Our PM's were due on our lifts. Clay @ Medley came out 8/19 and 8/20. Didn't see any issues with the tires on this lift. They aren't in the greatest shape. Due to the fact that we're getting rid of this lift before long, it's not worth replacing unless it puts the lift out of production. James @ Medley came out today for another issue and I had him check this lift as well. He sees no issues with continuing on the existing tires. | Preston Ellexson - 08/15/24 12:19:06 PM: I'm not seeing any big chunks of the wheel missing. There are some spots that don't look too good. I'm having Ryan monitor for any more issues like this. With this lift being replaced soon, I don't want to spend any money unless there is a bad wheel/caster, or out riggers casters moving. I will update again tomorrow after a day of driving.",[]
234,EQ ID 234,Stand-Up Forklift #2,Assembly,15359,04/14/2025,6. General Maint,Rhino reported that he was copper showing on his charging cord for the Assembly stand up forklift.,Closed and Completed,0,0.25,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/14/2025 06:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 04/14/25  5:45:25 AM: There was a little copper showing on the positive cable. Wrapped with insulation tape and then with electrical. No more issues with this.,[]
234,EQ ID 234,Stand-Up Forklift #2,Assembly,17018,09/17/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",We are experiencing some issues with the forklift in the Assembly area. It is not wanting to go into reverse. One of the tires are also starting to bald where the forklift is starting to slide when turning into the aisles.,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston/James@Medley/Eric@Medley,Maintenance,0,10/14/2025 01:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/15/25  4:28:51 AM: Eric came out to swap the tire on 10/7. The lift wasn't operational, so he just changed the tire in maintenance. James got parts in 10/10 and came out 10/14 to complete the repair. He replaced new parts. He had to adjust the switches a few times. Every time you tighten something up on that assembly, it changed the switches shift point from forward/neutral/reverse. He got the lift functioning good. When the caster swiveled from moving forward to reverse, it was out of alignment. He got this adjusted and tested. I also test drove the lift all around to ensure safety and functionality. Everything is working good. He put back on all covers and I sent the lift back to Jimmie for use. | Preston Ellexson - 09/30/25 10:09:52 AM: Parts were hard for Medley to track down. They got ordered this morning from 2 different vendors and James should receive them by end of day 10/3. He will be out 10/6 or 10/7 for this repair. | Preston Ellexson - 09/26/25  7:46:18 AM: James came out 9/22. He found a shaft and gear that are worn out. There is enough slop that it affects the forward/reverse contactor engaging and disengaging. He ordered the part and figured it would be here by end of the week 9/26. He will be back next week to repair this lift and get it operational. | Preston Ellexson - 09/18/25  7:35:54 AM: Lift was taken out of commission. The reverse issue is getting worse. I got with our tech and he can't make it until 9/22. He can get the reverse issue repaired or let me know what to order. I am getting parts ordered to have the tire replaced as well. | Preston Ellexson - 09/17/25  5:59:46 AM: Jimmie got with me on this. I will get with our tech James and see when he's available to come by and check it out.",[]
