236,EQ ID 236,Vendor Pem Stud Riveter,Assembly,20276,08/06/2026,1. Prod Stopped,Anvil on stud machine broke.,Closed and Completed,0,8,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/07/2026 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/07/26  7:46:34 AM: The bottom die was in bad shape. I made a new one out of the extra Scott bought designed for this application. It broke within days. Top die was in really bad shape when this one broke. I made new top and bottom dies. Made 3 of each. 2 spares for each now. I also hardened the 2 spares of each when I was finished machining them. I am going to see if Matt wants to hold onto them, or if he wants me to keep them. The top die will need a small shim stock added to the shaft because I couldn't make a locking collar slot on it. I just cut up some .0015 feeler gauge for a slight press fit application. There will be slight height adjustments that may be needed when changing to new dies. Shouldn't be enough to matter, but just in case, it'll need to be checked.",[]
