251,EQ ID 251,Vendor Spotwelder KVA-20 (#11218),Assembly,1550,06/02/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",welder not running correctly,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/02/2022 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/02/22 12:34:53 PM: Went over this morning and worked on the tip to get it welding good. Had to adjust the air pressure as well. They were still having problems prior to lunch, so I went over after lunch and we swapped out the welding tip. Got Mark to look at the fixture, since he is making duplicates, and to make adjustments so we don't have this problem near as much in the future.",[]
251,EQ ID 251,Vendor Spotwelder KVA-20 (#11218),Assembly,1638,06/10/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Spotwelder is lifting very slow.  Needs to be adjusted.,Closed and Completed,241,3.5,Mark Zeober,Maintenance,0,07/06/2022 08:30 AM,"Mark Zeober - 07/06/22  8:17:42 AM: The Pin wasn't broke.  After further investigation, I found that the Pin Bolt had backed out. I wasn't able to see this from the access point, I found out when I tried to remove it.  I tightened both Pin Bolts, & everything should be fine now. | Mark Zeober - 06/22/22 10:16:27 AM: David at Spotweld Consultants came in and we discovered one of the air lines had moved around so much that it put a kink in it, he also confirmed that the cylinder pin is broke. I repositioned the air hose and put a lose Zip tie to keep it from rotating.  David said he would look for a pin, but doubts he has one. the cylinder manufacture wont sell just the pin, so, we would have to remove the good pin, measure it, re-install the pin, then make a new one, and install the new one. | Mark Zeober - 06/21/22  8:52:11 AM: 7/16/22 removed cover and it looks like 1 of the cylinder end rod pins is broke. also while there I found several air leaks and a rotted out lubricator.  Bhumi called David at Spotweld Consultants to come look at the possible broken Pin.  6/21/22 Replaced Air Filter & Lubricator with ARO 2000 Series. and changed out all the leaking  fittings. | Preston Ellexson - 06/10/22  5:33:51 AM: Air pressure was adjusted up a little. We will monitor the machine for a few days.",[]
251,EQ ID 251,Vendor Spotwelder KVA-20 (#11218),Assembly,2052,08/01/2022,1. Prod Stopped,robos welders top arm came loose and is unsafe to operate,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Mark Zeober,Maintenance,2,08/01/2022 12:00 AM,"Mark Zeober - 08/05/22  6:39:24 AM: Bolt backed out pivot pin causing the pin on the other side to break off.  Modified the broken pin to accept a standard 1/2 - 13 bolt, we now have more thread engagement, & put lock tight the bolts. | Mark Zeober - 08/05/22  6:39:07 AM: Bolt backed out pivot pin causing the pin on the other side to break off.  Modified the broken pin to accept a standard 1/2 - 13 bolt, we now have more thread engagement, & put lock tight the bolts.",[]
