251,EQ ID 251,Vendor Spotwelder KVA-20 (#11218),Assembly,5536,05/03/2023,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",makes a clunking noise that is not normal for the machine.,Closed Without Action,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/26/2024 01:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/26/24 11:48:50 AM: We are in process of scheduling multiple cell moves to accommodate the new large trimline cell. We bought new machinery prior to knowing the PMU cells were going to combine. We will have extra welders. I'll put the 2 new ones in service and remove the 2 worst ones for backup, and parts. This machine will be one removed from service. | Preston Ellexson - 05/16/23  4:05:15 AM: Still awaiting parts. | Preston Ellexson - 05/03/23 10:43:29 AM: Removed cover to inspect while in operation. Ball joint knuckle is completely worn out again. I am getting with David @ Spotwelding Consultants for a quote.",[]
253,EQ ID 253,PMU 1 Spotwelder KVA-20 (#11220),Assembly,2482,10/03/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Check baron on welder,Closed and Completed,0,4.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/04/2022 11:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/04/22  9:48:17 AM: Got the machine put all back together and reset tip. Cleaned with a file to flatten. Tested and the machine is welding good. Released for production. | Preston Ellexson - 10/04/22  9:47:35 AM: The top arm has too much play in it left to right. Possible safety concern if the top arm slipped and missed the bottom tip. Removed needed covers and got the entire arm off the machine. The bushing are good. The shaft is good. Where the top arm mounts the shaft to the bearings has been worn down over the years. It needs to be replaced. I made come sleeves to put on both sides of the arm between the bearings. It will run this way for awhile, but I am getting a quote for a new top arm mount.",[]
