255,EQ ID 255,Large Trimline TIG Welder Syncrowave 250,Assembly,20050,07/08/2026,1. Prod Stopped,Tig gun in Large Trimline 2 is not welding,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/21/2026 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26  5:27:44 AM: The new guns were ordered. They had a 2-3 week lead time. Went to the machine. Tested the machine/gun. The machine is working fine. Inspected inside just to be safe. Found no issues, so I put all the covers back on. The gun operators in every other way with no issues. I took it apart to inspect. The red cable hose was connected with the tubing. Inside it was separated and this is why the gun was not working properly. Trimmed the line back and cleaned the threads on the brass connector. Tightened it and fit the hose to the connector. Got everything tight and fit back inside the gun. Put gun cover on and turned the machine on. I had the operator put new ceramic and tungsten in the gun. Tested with no issues. Welds are looking good. I believe this happened because we have the gun hanging from the ceiling by one point. This caused it to pull free internally since it couldn't sway. Got the lift over and refit the hanging points. It now has 2 like the large trimline cell. Everything is ready to use. | Dennis Davis - 07/08/26  7:27:36 AM: I am not getting any electrical continuity between the gun and the welder indicating that there is a broken wire and we need to replace
the leads. I will make sure that one is going to be ordered",[]
261,EQ ID 261,PMU 2 Spotwelder KVA-30 (#11233),Assembly,3446,12/05/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",2 Boats stripped out top arm,Closed and Completed,0,8,Preston,Maintenance,0,12/07/2022 03:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 12/08/22 12:43:12 PM: Removed the top cover and the top arm to allow for removal of the top arm holder. Brought to maintenance. It was stripped out on 3 bolts that were 7/16-14. I drilled and tapped out to a 9/16-12. Had to make new non-conductive washers and sleeves. I made them out of hard plastic stock. Cleaned burrs from holder and top arm. Took all back to machine and re-assembled with the bigger bolts. Tested machine and it is working really good.,[]
