1750,EQ ID 1750,Skirt Multicyl (Tigerstop),Assembly,19854,06/15/2026,1. Prod Stopped,The multicyl will not work. Lead tried to rest it and it will not operate at all.,Closed Without Action,0,0,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/15/2026 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 06/15/26 12:22:25 PM: I have a work order in place for this. I am closing without action and logging everything on the first one entered. I'll update Evon as well.,[]
1750,EQ ID 1750,Skirt Multicyl (Tigerstop),Assembly,19845,06/15/2026,1. Prod Stopped,Electric eyeglass is busted on Multicyl,Closed and Completed,2000,12,Preston/David@DCW,Maintenance,0,06/30/2026 11:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/09/26  6:59:52 AM: David came out and got this working good. He gave me a couple pointers to add more safety redundancy within the wiring as well. Everything is running as it should now. Curtains are functioning safely and wired safely as well. Machine is good for production. | Preston Ellexson - 06/30/26  5:34:48 AM: We went ahead and got a Keyence safety relay and light curtains. I removed the old set-up. I got everything drilled and tapped for the new curtain brackets and electrical junction box. Got the din rail mounted with the relay on it. Rewired coil pack, foot pedal and DC wires in the electrical junction box. I ran the air lines different from the valve. Removed the main valve and cleaned. Everything on it is good and functions without issue. Removed the coil pack and pneumatic valve to inspect and clean. No issues here either. Replaced the mufflers on the valve with new. Tested the machine without the safety relay just to make sure it functions as it should. No issues here. I went through the manual for the safety relay and the light curtains. Tried wiring, and I'm having issues with machine repeatability. Got with 2 techs at Keyence. They both had me try different ways to wire. It is still not working the way it should. The contacts that control the barrier being broken are NC. Most systems are NO. I believe this is causing a double redundancy issue that I can't figure out. I got with David@DCW Industrial Services. He flew in 6/29 and will be here this morning to help me get this wired up and running safely. | Preston Ellexson - 06/17/26  5:35:37 AM: I checked continuity and voltage on anything inside the Pinnacle light curtain box that could affect this. I am not seeing any issues, and it isn't throwing any error codes. Took the top off of the foot pedal. Only one switch is being used. I checked continuity and voltage on it with no inconsistencies. Took foot pedal behind the machine so I could troubleshoot while operating with the light curtain electrical box open. I am not finding any issues at all after running for 30+ minutes. I had the operator come over while I checked everything. 15 parts were ran. I told him to keep running and let Johnny know if it happened again. He welded up all the skirts, went over after break, and it wouldn't run. Aside from replacing the Pinnacle control box, there can't be anything else that would fix this. I received a quote 6/15 from Guardomation APS for a new emitter and receiver. I am awaiting a quote for a new control box. As soon as I receive this, I'll let Evon know we need to get it ordered ASAP. | Preston Ellexson - 06/17/26  4:35:20 AM: They are only having one issue with this I'm trying to troubleshoot. While in operation, the machine will randomly not operate. When this first started, the operator could simply break the light barrier, and the machine would continue. The operator deemed this unsafe to operator since he was intentionally having to break a safety barrier to get the machine to function properly. I locked the machine out. Removed the coil pack and valve and brought to maintenance. Left the solenoid connector tied in. Took apart the coil pack. One of the internal springs seemed to be out of place. I got it all cleaned, dried, and re-assembled. Put back on the machine. Tested for 30-40 minutes with no issues. I tried to make it fault out with no luck. Let the operator run. It wasn't long before Johnny called back with the same issue. | Preston Ellexson - 06/15/26 12:19:06 PM: Work is in progress. I have quotes in process while I troubleshoot.",[]
