1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,9658,01/10/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Controller motor is stuck,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/29/2024 09:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 01/30/24  6:22:15 AM: Sprayed the ball screw for the foam control to ease up during operation. Cleaned jaws and replaced all teflon tape. Replaced the cut wire too. Got back together and still have issues with the film rolling straight. Replaced the entire jaw assembly and got all put back together. Adjusted recipe and machine is running good. I need to repair the rollers/bearings on the assembly I removed in maintenance. | Preston Ellexson - 01/22/24  6:39:47 AM: Getting with Johnny on this machine to see about urgency on repair.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,10623,03/04/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door not kitchen magnet,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/04/2024 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/07/24  5:15:52 AM: Operators cleaned the door parts of the machine and it has been running good for 2 days now. | Preston Ellexson - 03/04/24 11:48:29 AM: Adjusted door pressure and recipe. Still same issue. Swapped the load cell for the door out, reset door pressure, and still the same outcome. Got with Ronnie to see if it might be a board issue. Machine is running, the molds just don't look too good.",[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,8190,11/30/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door motor come apart,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/12/2024 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 03/12/24  8:19:03 AM: Completed this awhile back. Went ahead and swapped the entire jaw assembly. The motor wasn't the only repair needed. There are bearings inside the aluminum roller that need replaced. The labor takes an hour or 2 to removed everything and get all replaced. I have the old jaw assembly in maintenance for repair. Machine has been running good since.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,10775,03/20/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Mode pressure iow,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/21/2024 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 03/26/24  4:37:27 AM: Inspected machine. Ran diagnostics and found a leak on the tank. Turned everything off and locked out. Removed tank and took to maintenance. Ground off paint and welded all bad spots. Came in next morning and cleaned up weld. Put tank back on machine and got everything plugged back in. Tested and  now everything looks good. I adjusted the coupler on the calendar motor due to it moving away from the jaw coupler. Got cover put back on. Had to adjust the recipe. Got code from Ronnie to adjust main settings. Adjusted the reverse distance on the film after a cycle. Made minor adjustments while the machine was warming up and everything looks good.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,11090,04/12/2024,1. Prod Stopped,Blown views,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/12/2024 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/12/24 12:15:02 PM: Replaced fuse. Tested vacuum motor with new fuse and my meter on it. Brushes on vacuum motor are no good, and they're not replaceable. I swapped the vacuum motor out with a new one, and replaced the fuse again. Tested with no issues. Made some adjustments on the film speed start and the reverse distance on the film. It has been running good with no more issues.",[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,11713,05/16/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,needs general maintenance,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/16/2024 01:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 05/23/24  5:36:33 AM: So far this machine hasn't had any other issues. Got with Matt this morning on it. We did receive in warranty stock parts for the IMolds though. Machine is good. | Preston Ellexson - 05/16/24 12:06:57 PM: Had to remove brackets for the A/B hoses. Pulled back up and tightened brackets. The lines have just slipped down over time. Moved the assembly in and out manually to see if it would still hit. Had to adjust the metal flex arm out a little bit. Ran a leak test with no issues. Compressor is working good. Adjusted the recipe and cleaned the teflon tape up. Machine is running ok. It is taking longer than normal to initiate the release of the mold after it is completed. It might be a board going out. I need to order some parts tomorrow for stock. I will monitor this and leave it open until next week.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,12484,07/22/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,controller calendar motor issues,Closed and Completed,0,5,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/23/2024 01:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/23/24 12:09:49 PM: Inspected machine. A/B lines were pretty tight in the mount by the electrical box. Got some slack in them and put a zip tie on for a stop. Cleaned cut wire and teflon. Put on a new teflon apron due to one missing. Tested and we were still getting the calendar motor error off and on. I replaced the calendar motor with a new one and got mounted back on. Door pressure was high so I adjusted it down. Made minor adjustments to the recipe. Replaced FE circuit board due to multiple errors that point towards this. Added dispenser solution. Replaced main film roll. Got machine running good molds with very little issues. Cables for lift table were smashed by the table. Up/Down control has been locked out because it's broken. Went ahead and replaced the control and cable. Replaced the power cable with new. It was wired in a box via wire nuts. Turned power off, removed, and put on a plug so it could be unplugged if needed. Machine is now running good and lift table works.",[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,12557,07/29/2024,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",low pressure error and door not operating properly.,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/26/2024 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/31/24  7:31:59 AM: Inspected machine. There is a precharge error coming up. This happens because the machine will stop in the middle of a mold, and never eject. There is still air in the tank when it tries to start a new mold but gets confused on tank pressure. When this error happens, you just have to remove the tubing from the tank and let it bled out. Started up the mold. Still getting door issues even after adjusting. I removed the back door cover and replaced the load cell. Adjusted door pressure and hit run. After adjusting the recipe and cleaning the machine pretty well, it's running good. I let it run and came back to check every hour. Machine hasn't had anymore issues yet.",[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,12659,08/06/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,I believe air compressor is going out,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/06/2024 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 08/09/24 12:41:50 PM: Had to replace compressor. Adjusted recipe. Everything else was good. Monitored for a few hours off and on with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 08/06/24 12:40:08 PM: Work in process.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,12892,08/28/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,i think the blower motor burnt up after replacing fuse?,Closed and Completed,0,10,Preston/Ronnie @ Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,09/23/2024 02:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/25/24 10:46:15 AM: Received parts and Ronnie came back out 9/23 to complete. Got board replaced and re-programmed machine. Replaced the vacuum motor too. Tested with no issues. Machine is good to run. | Preston Ellexson - 09/19/24  5:40:40 AM: Had Ronnie come out. After troubleshooting for awhile, he's fairly certain he found the problem. The small board with the 2-30A fuses in the back console is the power management board. He thinks this is the culprit. He ordered 2 overnight, but they probably won't be here until Friday. He said you have to re-program the machine after this is swapped out, so he'll have to come back to complete repair. | Preston Ellexson - 08/29/24  8:53:17 AM: Checked voltage and everything is good incoming. Removed the cover off of the console cover behind machine. Found a capacitor that had burned up for some reason. Outgoing voltage was lost and only about 6V per each leg. Verified on another machine just to be certain. Got with Ronnie and he overnighted a new console circuit board. I will swap out when it arrives. Machine is locked out and all tools, etc. were removed. | Preston Ellexson - 08/28/24  6:34:36 AM: Checked vacuum motor. Brushes are burnt up pretty bad. Replaced vacuum motor with new. Turned on power and still have a black screen. I believe we blew the power supply which probably caused a current spike that took the vacuum motor. I am finishing another job and getting back on this today.",[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,14097,12/16/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Getting too much foam,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston/Ronnie @ Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,12/19/2024 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 12/31/24  6:23:28 AM: Ronnie came out and got this fixed. He programmed all the new molds while he was here so we should be able to run any mold on any machine. Adjustments will need to be made to the recipe if ran on different machines.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,14496,01/28/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Sensor not working foam machine in paint cell,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/28/2025 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 01/30/25  8:54:51 AM: Replaced teflon on jaw and sealing bar. Adjusted the cut seal percentage due to it being too hot. Adjusted the door percentage to swing open quicker. Adjusted to recipe until molds looked good. Replaced 2 of the teflon aprons. Machine is running good molds.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,16597,08/07/2025,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,blower motor is not working mother board is probably fried after some diagnosis was done.,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/07/2025 08:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 08/08/25  4:34:32 AM: Turned machine on. Tested compressor and it's working good. Nothing when I run the vacuum motor though. Tested voltage and the board isn't sending out voltage the way it should. Turned off power and swapped FE board. Turned machine on. Tested vacuum motor with no issues. They had just replaced this one too so brushes are almost brand new. Started running machine. Got recipe adjusted. Adjusted door pressure. Machine is running good with no issues.,[]
1886,EQ ID 1886,PMU 1 Foam Machine,Assembly,16783,08/22/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",film will not dispense properly to allow machine to run.,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston/Matt,Maintenance,0,09/01/2025 06:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 09/09/25  8:51:28 AM: Matt swapped out the jaw assembly with a new one. Machine is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 08/28/25  4:05:06 AM: Machine has a bearing locked up on a roller. It won't even roll in the machine. Removed jaw assembly and brought to maintenance. Found that the aluminum roller bearing on the right side was locked up. Removed everything and replaced with new. Put back on machine. For some reason it still is wanting to backfeed the film on the right side. I had Dan send a new jaw assembly. It should be here today. I will replace this when it arrives and go from there. | Dennis Davis - 08/25/25  4:04:23 AM: looking into this,[]
