1893,EQ ID 1893,Lift Table (Large Trimline),Assembly,16645,08/12/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,"The lift table started having a strong wire burning smell, per Preston could be out of oil or motor issue.",Closed and Completed,760,5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/17/2025 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/17/25  9:51:10 AM: Finally got this knocked out. Checked motor wiring before installing. Got a new gasket made for the pump to motor mount. Got pump mounted to motor and installed back on the lift table. Got hydraulic lines tightened. Rewired pump and motor in electrical box. Removed foot pedals and took apart. Checked switches and they look good. Mounted all back on and tightened electrical lines. Plugged lift table in, removed maintenance stop, and tested up and down numerous times. Lift table is working good with no issues. Had Jimmie take back to LTL 2. Got it setup, plugged in, and tested again. Good to use for production. | Preston Ellexson - 08/25/25  5:28:38 AM: Received the motor in 8/22. I'll get this done when I can. This week is busy. | Preston Ellexson - 08/20/25  4:23:28 AM: Finally got the motor ordered yesterday afternoon. It will make it here next week and I'll proceed with this repair. | Preston Ellexson - 08/15/25  8:51:35 AM: Made notes of electrical wiring and disconnected motor assembly. Got it removed from the lift table. Oil isn't the issue. It is relatively clean too. Took the pump off the motor. Pump is still moving free with no issues. Motor is completely shot. Windings on top and bottom caught on fire inside the motor. Not sure why this happened but I'm checking the foot switches and the rest of the electrical for any issues. Got a quote from Presto for a new motor. Awaiting a call to place the credit card order today. I will inspect the electrical before the motor arrives. 1-3 day lead time so it'll be end of next week before it arrives. | Preston Ellexson - 08/12/25 12:28:49 PM: Went to LTL 2 cell. Lift table motor is extremely hot. It either ran low on oil, or locked up for some other reason. Tripped the breaker. I reset it. No power issues just the table. I will inspect this first thing tmrw. It smells too bad right now. I'll see if I can find a motor/gear box replacement or a lift table replacement after inspection.",[]
