1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,5689,05/16/2023,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required","fried the 901 control box, pulled away from the machine via power cord.",Closed and Completed,0,5,Preston/Ronnie,Maintenance,0,05/24/2023 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 05/31/23 12:05:26 PM: Swapped compressor and small 1164FE board. Still not getting A or B in bag. Pressure error. Ronnie came in the next week and got it all running. He had to use a new main board and transfer all the files via usb flash drive. After adjusting recipe he got machine running good. | Preston Ellexson - 05/19/23  5:06:31 AM: Received in the replacement power console. Got it all swapped out and inspected everything else on the machine. Visually everything else looks good. Turned on and tested. Compressor isn't making any psi. New ones will be here today and I'll continue to see if there are any other parts that need replaced.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,6083,06/16/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door open before finish,Closed Without Action,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/22/2023 06:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/14/23 11:30:25 AM: Duplicate work order. | Preston Ellexson - 06/22/23  4:11:47 AM: Ronnie looked into this and is thinking the magnet is just getting weak. I will swap and go from there. | Preston Ellexson - 06/20/23  4:08:37 AM: Tried many things troubleshooting. Called Ronnie @ Sealed Air and we tested a few more things. No changes overall. I put this mold back in large trimline and started it up. No issues at all. Put a small mold in this machine and we are not having the door issues. I let Ronnie know so he can figure out what issue we have going on. I am awaiting a response, but both machines are running good right now.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,7994,11/10/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Air Compressor Fail,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/10/2023 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 11/14/23  4:55:04 AM: Tested machine and the compressor isn't even kicking on. Got it swapped out with a new one. Changed filters and all. Don't see any other issues with the machine. Turned on and got running. Had to finish this on Monday to make sure the recipe didn't need any adjustments. I did adjust a few things but everything is running good now.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,10827,03/26/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Losing charge,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/21/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/27/24 10:31:52 AM: Replaced compressor. Replaced board due to more issues. Checked bloffer and vacuum motor. Checked calendar motor coupler. Replaced some teflon on the jaw assembly due to bad sealing of film. Adjusted door pressure. After adjusting the recipe quite a bit, I had to adjust the film reverse distance after the film seals every cycle. Got the machine running and sealing good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,10842,03/28/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Cross seal wire open,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/03/2024 09:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/04/24  4:08:13 AM: Turned on machine and inspected. I didn't see anything visually wrong with the cross seal wire, but the error happens the first time and stays. I went ahead and swapped the jaw out with a used one from maintenance. The teflon and wire are pretty new, so it should last for awhile. Made recipe adjustments and everything is running good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,11091,04/12/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Film hang up on one side,Closed Without Action,0,0,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/23/2024 07:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 05/23/24  5:39:30 AM: This is not an issue on the machine. I fixed this when I worked on it last. Got with Matt today and he said all the IMolds are running good and need no work right now.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,13127,09/20/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,controller arm fell down,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/20/2024 01:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 09/25/24 10:41:33 AM: Inspected machine. The dispenser assembly had come loose. It only holds in place with one thumb screw on the right side. It had worked its way loose and the assembly fell out of the dowel pin holes. Put back in place and tightened thumb screw. Machine is ready to run.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,13923,11/26/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,air tank is cracked.,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston/Derek,Maintenance,0,12/02/2024 12:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 12/09/24  4:23:47 AM: Removed tank and brought to maintenance. I welded up one we already had in back and put on this machine. One is still in need of repair. Got all the lines plugged back in the machine and turned on. Did a leak test and everything is good.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,13963,12/04/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,not putting foam in a bag.,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston/Derek,Maintenance,0,12/06/2024 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 12/09/24  4:20:21 AM: Replaced the dispenser head assembly. Cleaned fittings on A and B hoses while they were disconnected. Combed through the lines to the dispenser. They were tangled and zip tied that way. Got everything swapped out and started. Made minor adjustments to the recipe and everything is running good.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,14515,01/29/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,foam machine problem that you looked at yesterday.,Closed Without Action,0,0,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/30/2025 09:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 01/30/25  8:51:05 AM: Operators are saying the machine is running good with no issues.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,14617,02/10/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",head not going back in,Closed and Completed,0,2.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,02/11/2025 07:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 02/11/25  5:54:15 AM: Matt was having a hard time getting the mixing block back in the machine. I test fit a new mixing block with no issues. This tells me the ball screw controlling the mixing block is faulty and not opening at the right height anymore. I removed the entire dispenser assembly and replaced with a new one. Replaced power cable too. Fixed mounts for the hoses/lines going to the head. Replaced missing bolts on the mounts as well. The dispenser assembly was a little rough while manually moving in and out. Sprayed ball screw with white lithium grease. Turned machine on and tested everything with no issues. Made adjustments to the recipe and everything is working good right now. Good molds.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,14328,01/13/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",put new filters and cleaned.  but it is still showing dispenser solution high pressure.,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,02/14/2025 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 02/05/25  7:56:12 AM: Changed dispenser solution assembly. Changed the mixing block. Replaced teflon on both sides of the jaw assembly. Got the code from Dan to go into the settings. Lowered the seal wire percentage because we're going through them much quicker than in the past. Adjusted the dispenser solution pressure. After getting those set I started running molds. Adjusted recipe and got everything working good. Machine is making good molds.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,14761,02/19/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,lost power,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,02/19/2025 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 02/20/25  8:21:56 AM: Removed cover from rear console. Main 30A fuses were still good. 10A glass fuse was blown. Swapped with new and started machine. Swapped mold handle block because one was broken. Put mold in they needed and got recipe adjusted. Molds are running good.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,15065,03/14/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Lost power,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/14/2025 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/18/25  4:19:12 AM: Removed cover on rear console. 10A glass fuse inside connector was blown. Swapped out and turned machine on. Went to run first mold. Film comes down, A/B fill, no vacuum, no door, then we lose power. Checked the fuse and it was burnt up again. I smelled a burning smell after it shut down. Swapped vacuum motor and no more issues. Brushes on the other one were no good causing excess current. Got covers put back on and mold running. After adjusting the recipe, the machine is running good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,15441,04/21/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required","door motor going out, binding up",Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/21/2025 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25  4:18:52 AM: Went to the machine. The door motor lovejoy coupler was not engaged with the door gear. Set screws were loose on both lovejoys. Got set back where they need to be. Tightened both set screws. Replaced jaw with rebuilt. Bottom wire was starting to show and cause film seal issues. Door was randomly trying to open during operation. Found the mag block had loose bolts. Removed the left side cover and tightened both allen shoulder screws. Replaced brass plate shim stock. Put cover back on. Door is staying shut now with no issues. Made recipe adjustments and let run. Machine is doing good making good molds.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,17037,09/18/2025,2. General Maint - High Priority,wires are exposed on the arm and need replaced. machine is locked out currently,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/18/2025 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 09/18/25 12:33:39 PM: Cable going to the mixing block assembly had multiple exposed wires. No arc flash or anything major. Got cable swapped out with a new one. Routed all cables together and tightened everything up. Removed lock and turned on power. Removed cover and adjusted door pressure. It was extremely low. Put cover back on. Bled air from tank. Calibrated eject cycle. Started running and molds are looking pretty good. No change in recipe. After everything warmed up molds are looking good. No more issues.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,17133,10/03/2025,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required","replaced the door, the door now works but it is still not functioning right.  as per our conversation its probably a mother board is faulty.",Closed Without Action,0,0,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/06/2025 06:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 10/06/25  4:33:53 AM: I have another work order in place for this. I will update the existing work order.,[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,17047,09/19/2025,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,"door not closing, and trying to eject foam before its time.",Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/07/2025 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/07/25  7:41:47 AM: With the issues they've been having, I replaced the FE circuit board with a new one. Turned machine on and tested. Getting calendar motor error. Removed cover and found a pretty good gap between the lovejoy couplers. Adjusted motor side and shaft side. Tightened set screws and fed film. This took care of that error. Calibrated eject cycle with no issues. Checked recipe and it looks good. Started running and machine didn't have any issues. Waited until everything warmed up. Recipe is running good. Machine isn't having any issues. | Preston Ellexson - 10/06/25  4:30:04 AM: They got the door in and got it swapped out. Machine is still not operational. They have a new work order in for this. I will continue this work order and close the other as a duplicate. | Preston Ellexson - 09/30/25  8:17:58 AM: Checked machine before turning on. Everything is ready. Turned machine on, checked recipe, and started mold. Door didn't want to close. Mold was also trying to eject before the cycle was complete. Went to operations to test the door. It opens with no problem. It won't close at all. The motor engages and ""jogs"" the door, but it won't shut. Brass bushing are in really bad shape. Gears show signs of wear through broken teeth in some places. Without the door working, I can't look further into why the cycle is wanting to eject early. Got with Dan@Sealed Air. He has a door assembly coming. It won't process and ship until 9/30. I told Matt he could swap it out when it arrives or just wait until I come back 10/6.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,17230,10/09/2025,6. General Maint,film not wanting to roll out seems tight Mabey in a bind,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/13/2025 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/13/25  5:40:00 AM: Opened cover and removed right side film roll bracket. The spring tension is on a threaded stud weld. There are  pieces that thread on it that are flat but can thread onto the stud fully. They just needed adjusted so the threads were flush instead of protruding out. Both threads were rubbing the film as it fed down. Got these adjusted and put the bracket back on. Got film ready, checked recipe, and started mold. Everything is feeding good now. Let it warm up and recipe is making good molds. Machine is good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,17856,12/08/2025,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,NOT HOLDING AIR PRESSURE,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,02/12/2026 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 02/16/26  6:34:22 AM: Tank had a leak. Removed it and brought to maintenance. Welded top of the tank up and ground smooth. Swapped out air fitting on bottom. Someone broke the other one and put on different fittings to reduce the tubing size. Put the tank back on the machine. Turned on and calibrated eject cycle with no issues. Checked recipe and it looks good. Everything else on the machine looks good as well. Started making molds. After everything warmed up, the machine is running good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,19921,06/22/2026,2. General Maint - High Priority,corner foam mold blew apart. the plastic part separated from the wood.,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/23/2026 11:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26  5:41:28 AM: Took the mold apart and cleaned everything as much as I could. Scraped a lot of the build-up off. Put back together the edge screws. They were still holding good. For all the broken holes, I put broken toothpicks in. I replaced the screws as well. Used epoxy when putting back together. I only used a little in every hole. I hope with the toothpicks will help this all hold longer. Got all back tight and left to dry overnight in maintenance. Got with Matt and he had me put it in the small trimline cell for future use. Mold is good.",[]
1919,EQ ID 1919,PMU 2 Foam Machine,Assembly,20466,08/24/2026,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,Air tank cracked.,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/25/2026 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/25/26  7:32:00 AM: Tank was cracked at the top. Turned machine off. Removed the rear console cover and ground wire on back and set aside. Removed bloffer, vacuum motor, and air lines from the tank. Unbolted tank and used a shop vac to clean out all debris. Ran a tap through the tank mounting holes to clean. Put repaired tank on and got bolted up. Put on air lines, bloffer, and vacuum motor. Put ground wire back on rear console cover. Put cover on and plugged everything back in. Turned the machine on and calibrated ejection. Started running at the end of the day. Came in 8/25 to get with Josh and see how it ran. He said it did good. I made some adjustments to the recipe. Cleaned up all debris in front of the machine. Molds are looking good. No more issues right now. | Preston Ellexson - 08/24/26  7:40:57 AM: I am checking the tank. We have one I've already repaired in maintenance I can swap with if needed.",[]
