1928,EQ ID 1928,Pallet Jack,Assembly,18518,02/19/2026,6. General Maint,Pallet jack in skirt cell,Closed and Completed,0,1,Dennis Davis,Maintenance,0,03/04/2026 10:00 AM,"Dennis Davis - 03/04/26  8:01:52 AM: The tote lift has been scrapped, and a new one has been ordered | Dennis Davis - 02/25/26 11:59:35 AM: Waiting on Randall Garza to decide whether or not to fix or scrap | Dennis Davis - 02/24/26 10:32:36 AM: This pallet jack has several problems, and I am working with Scott to see if we are going to fix them or replace it.",[]
1941,EQ ID 1941,Sweat Bee Fan,Assembly,11729,05/17/2024,6. General Maint,separate power switch,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/17/2024 11:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/20/24  4:17:39 AM: Added another disconnect box so we could separate the fans. They just wanted the fan for the small trimline extension cell to be on its own. Spotweld cell is 2 disconnects. Got everything mounted, ran, wires extended and re-routed. Tested and everything is working good.",[]
1941,EQ ID 1941,Sweat Bee Fan,Assembly,20664,09/10/2026,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",the center fan is making a really bad noise from what sharron said,Pending,0,0.25,Dennis,Maintenance,0,09/11/2026 09:00 AM,"Dennis Davis - 09/11/26  9:39:43 AM: The fan sounds like it has a bad bearing so I unwired it so we can run the second fan until we have a chance to replace it | Preston Ellexson - 09/10/26  2:00:02 PM: Sharon got with me before I left. I turned the fan on to see what it sounded like. It's either a loose bolt causing the guard to rattle, or we have some sort of motor issue. I locked this out. I am busy tomorrow for most of the day already. I will get with Dennis first thing tomorrow to see if he has time to check this out.",[]
