1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1264,05/02/2022,1. Prod Stopped,Film rose up in the machine,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/03/2022 02:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/05/22  5:00:00 AM: Got bearings swapped out. Re-assembled unit. Took back to large trimline and got machine back together. Turned on and ran. Everything looks good and is functioning properly. | Preston Ellexson - 05/02/22 12:33:06 PM: One of the rollers on the head assembly isn't turning both ways. Removed the head assembly and brought to maintenance. Took all the way apart and cleaned. Found bad bearings on roller. Ordered from McMaster Carr and they'll be here tomorrow. I'll replaced bearings and re-assemble head unit. Hopefully that is the only issue, and we will have it back up and running.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1383,05/12/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Need lot of work,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/12/2022 07:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/12/22  6:43:00 AM: Changed the mixing block. Cleaned the head for the mixing block after removing the old one. The valve for the B line going into the mixing block is pretty hard to turn. I am going to see if Ronnie can order us another head. Once it arrives, I'll swap it out, clean the old one, and then we should have a backup on hand. Machine is running good now.",[]
