1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,5218,04/11/2023,1. Prod Stopped,MOLD EJECT,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/11/2023 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/12/23 12:03:08 PM: This was for small trimline machine. Changed out the mixing block. Nothing else is stopped up or too bad. Put on a rebuilt bloffer, epoxy on foam repair. Had to make adjustments to the corner mold, and then swap with small trimline mold and adjust it as well. Machine has ran good since with no other issues.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,5687,05/16/2023,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,error code will not clear,Closed Without Action,0,0.25,Matt,Maintenance,0,05/16/2023 12:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 05/16/23 11:06:30 AM: Operators got machine running. Dispenser solution was low so they filled. They said the screen had a message come up but everything was black so they couldn't see it. They turned machine power on and off a few times and everything is working good now. I will monitor for a few days to see if we need to get another display on order.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,6076,06/15/2023,2. General Maint - High Priority,not reaching precharge pressure. put new blopper in with no luck and air compresser seems fine.,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/19/2023 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 06/20/23  4:09:27 AM: Got this set back up and the machine/mold are running good so far. | Preston Ellexson - 06/16/23  8:17:57 AM: Ran a leak test and it was good. I don't feel or see any cracks on the tank. It's meeting the pressure requirements of the machine. I adjusted the recipe for awhile. Walked away and it threw a pressure error. Went back and they had moved the needed mold to another cell. I am waiting until they need this machine and have a mold setup to continue troubleshooting.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,6146,06/21/2023,1. Prod Stopped,Door won't close,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/21/2023 01:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/22/23  4:10:41 AM: The coupler for the motor and gear had come apart and weren't engaging. Adjusted and tightened the set screw bolts. Couldn't get the broken bolt out of the cover. We had a used cover in maintenance I swapped with. Adjusted the recipe, but the film wasn't cutting good every time. Replaced the strip on the jaw assembly with a new one. Cleaned cut wire. Got the recipe set pretty good. Machine is good.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,6231,06/27/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Tank Lincoln air,Closed and Completed,0,1,Josh Patton,Maintenance,0,06/27/2023 12:00 AM,,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,6428,07/14/2023,2. General Maint - High Priority,foam machine is down,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/19/2023 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/19/23 10:48:01 AM: Swapped the main GD board and the compressor. Had to re-calibrate the screen and manually load in the saved recipes. Got all back together and opened a door cover to clean out the foam. Found the bottom door mount was broken. The plates that hold the bushing had broken welds and separated. Got all cleaned up and welded back. Tested machine after everything was done and all is running good now. | Preston Ellexson - 07/14/23 11:25:08 AM: Getting 102-3 and 102-5 precharge and full pressure drop errors. Checked voltage, and when the signal sends for the compressor and vacuum motor to engage, they aren't. I swapped the vacuum motor, but that's not the issue. I'm fairly certain the main GD board needs replaced. We are out so I sent Ronnie a list to order for us. One is being sent overnight and will be here Monday. The only other issue could be the compressor, but I am starting with the board when it arrives and working from there.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,7194,09/12/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Magnet not on door,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/12/2023 10:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/13/23  4:06:36 AM: Door would shortly after mold starts. Error 122 Mold door has not reached closed position. Door pressure was very low. Adjusted it, but still happening. Checked FE board for anything. Removed cover for the door motor. The wiring harness for the closed sensor was partially unplugged. Refit all harnesses and tested. After adjusting mold for a bit, everything is running good.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,7463,10/04/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Foam blew up in the machine,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/04/2023 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 10/06/23  7:46:52 AM: Cleaned everything off. Removed jaw assembly and cleaned what needed. Replaced the liner and filter in the dispenser tray. Replaced the mixing block due to the mess. Tested and everything is working. Molds are looking pretty good.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,7816,10/27/2023,1. Prod Stopped,Door not opening,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/27/2023 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/27/23 12:03:59 PM: Checked door sensors, and they are all good. Nothing is loose. Checked door pressure, and it was pretty low. Adjusted and monitored machine during recipe adjustments. Had to put on a new roll of film and let it warm back up. Machine is running pretty good molds and no errors right now.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,8057,11/16/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",TO much foam,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/16/2023 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 11/17/23  7:01:48 AM: Step 4 was shooting foam on this one. Only steps 2 and 3 shoot foam on a 4 step recipe. Made adjustments to the recipe while running. Molds are good and machine is running good.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,9994,01/17/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Film hanging up wont roll down,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/17/2024 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 01/17/24  7:33:21 AM: Swapped out the dispenser assembly and ran the new power line back. Removed the teflon tape strips and the mounting plate. There was a bunch of mold inside causing the roller to lock up. Got everything clean and moving freely. Got all parts back on the machine and swapped molds out to run. After adjusting the recipe, all is running good.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,10103,01/25/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",IS not blowing foam bag out,Closed and Completed,0,6,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/25/2024 11:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 01/25/24 10:35:27 AM: Cleaned the excess foam off of the machine. Put on a new cut wire, teflon tape kit, door load cell, brass door shim plate, and new FE circuit board. Adjusted door pressure and recipe. Ran for awhile, but they started having issues with the air. Tested eject cycle and compressor wouldn't make psi. Replaced compressor with new and put on a new bloffer. Cycled machine power. Calibrated the eject cycle with no issues and no air leaks. Machine has ran over 75 pieces with no issues.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,10164,01/30/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door open early,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/30/2024 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 02/02/24  5:36:03 AM: Machine is still running good. | Preston Ellexson - 01/31/24  4:37:58 AM: Adjusted door pressure and tested. Ran many molds with no issues, but I am following up with Andrew shortly to see how it ran on overtime.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,10763,03/19/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Losing air,Closed Without Action,0,0,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/22/2024 11:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 03/22/24  9:43:31 AM: Duplicate work order.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,10321,02/12/2024,1. Prod Stopped,CALENDER MOTOR,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/15/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/22/24  8:32:49 AM: Finally got to this repair. There were a lot of parts that needed replaced since the initial calendar motor. Removed complete jaw assembly and brought to maintenance. Took all the way apart. Replaced outer mounted bearings for the black rubber roller. Replaced both black knurled rollers. Replaced bearings in the aluminum housing on the roller assembly. Cleaned most of the build-up on the jaw assembly. Got all back together and took back to machine. Replaced calendar motor. Replaced film motor. Replaced teflon strip on the jaw. Replaced one edge seal insert. Turned machine on and let it warm up. Adjusted recipe. Adjusted door pressure. Started machine and after making a few more adjustments, everything is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 02/16/24  6:42:35 AM: Got with Johnny on this. The calendar motor needs replaced. If he holds it in the right position when the machine is first turned on, it will run fine. The motor has come loose from it's housing like they have in the past. I will get to this next week sometime.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,11844,05/28/2024,1. Prod Stopped,Will not blow out bag,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/28/2024 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/29/24  4:09:01 AM: Tank had a crack in the top again. As I was removing the tank, the 120V cord for the lift table shorted out. Locked out plug and machine power. Removed tank and repaired in maintenance. Put back on machine after it cooled down. Repaired the power cord to the lift table. Repaired the incoming 120V plug due to wires showing. Got everything back together on the machine. Replaced the bracket for the A/B hoses on the side. One of the bolts was stripped out on the old one, and the rubber inside was gone. Got the door pressure adjusted. Recipe was good. Machine is running good parts.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12139,06/18/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Losing air,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/21/2024 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/26/24  5:54:38 AM: Replaced tank and fittings. Got all put back together, but they are low on the A-side drums right now. They started machine up this week and haven't had any issues out of it so far. | Preston Ellexson - 06/18/24 11:07:50 AM: Tank has a leak. Had Ronnie from Sealed Air order some last Friday. One will be in tomorrow and another will be in next week for stock.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12512,07/24/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,not sensing the film with full roll and the door is not opening.,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/29/2024 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/29/24  8:18:59 AM: Inspected machine. There were others issues that I found while waiting for the front film sensor to error out again. Door pressure needed adjusted. Recipe was adjusted numerous times. The door wouldn't stay shut with the right pressure setting. Ended up replacing the door pressure load sensor. When I was putting the door cover back on, some of the screws wouldn't start. Re-tapped threads on all door cover screws. Came back 7/29 and they were running a different mold. This was a very big mold, so it took a little longer fine tuning the recipe. Didn't get the film error, but the error log was full of this one. Removed front cover on the door. Adjusted the sensitivity on the front film sensor. Put cover back on and turned machine on. Got warmed up and molds are looking good. No issues right now.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12660,08/06/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Film not present,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/06/2024 01:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/09/24 12:43:20 PM: Removed front cover. Adjusted sensor multiple times. Sensor is faulty, but it is in a good position right now. We haven't gotten that error in a day or so. I will order a new one next week when I return. Adjusted door pressure. Adjusted recipe on mold. Machine is running good right now. | Preston Ellexson - 08/09/24 12:43:12 PM: Removed front cover. Adjusted sensor multiple times. Sensor is faulty, but it is in a good position right now. We haven't gotten that error in a day or so. I will order a new one next week when I return. Adjusted door pressure. Adjusted recipe on mold. Machine is running good right now. | Preston Ellexson - 08/06/24 12:40:34 PM: Work in process.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12841,08/22/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Solution tray stopped up,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/22/2024 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24 12:31:23 PM: Took solution tray and drain line off. Brought to maintenance and fully cleaned. They are running without filters because they don't have any. Put all back on. Cut a scotch brite filter out of our stock and put in tray. Had to replace the door pressure load cell due to issues with the door opening. Adjusted the recipe a few times and got everything running good. | Preston Ellexson - 08/22/24  9:36:18 AM: Work in process.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12857,08/23/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door open early,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/23/2024 01:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 08/23/24 12:24:49 PM: Adjusted door pressure. Adjusted recipe to help. Ran over 60 without any door issues.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,13823,11/14/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Burn out on roller,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/10/2025 06:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/10/25  4:33:08 AM: This has been fixed for a couple weeks now. Originally went over and replaced door assembly due to bad bushings on the door. Replaced teflon and teflon aprons. Once I got everything replaced, the machine was just stopping as soon as it was supposed to shoot A/B chemicals. Got with Dan and tech support. They suggested swapping boards out. Swapped out main with new. Didn't have a memory card that would fit it. Dumped files and cleaned the old card. Loaded with updated recipes and tried running. Still the same thing. Swapped FE board with new and still no change. Got with Dan and tech support again. They suggested swapping FE board. After swapping 2 new FE boards, machine started running good. Made recipe adjustments and door pressure adjustments. First time I've had a bad FE board.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,15149,03/24/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Back roller hanging up,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/31/2025 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/31/25  5:25:08 AM: Removed jaw assembly and brought to maintenance. Removed everything and inspected. Black rollers are working still. Aluminum roller bearings are still really good. Cleaned everything, and lubed all bearings with white lithium grease. Put all back together and took to machine. Put on and got going. Still doing the same thing on the left side. Removed and brought to maintenance again. Took apart and replaced the left side black knurled roller and put all back together. Sprayed some lithium grease on again when putting back together. Put back on the machine. It is doing much better. Should've replaced both rollers, but didn't have the needed parts. Got recipe adjusted and everything is running good. I am ordering a list of replacement parts from Sealed Air today.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,15414,04/17/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Back roller hanging up,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/21/2025 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25  4:12:53 AM: Removed jaw assembly. Replaced with one newly rebuilt. Ran a few molds and got a high pressure reading. The mixing block was completed stopped up and was everywhere on the dispenser assembly. Removed the block and trashed. Removed the drain line and cleaned fully. Cleaned the mixing block tray. Replaced both filters. Cleaned the dispenser assembly. Replaced mixing block with new. Got all done and started machine again. Made adjustments to recipe. Got the machine running really good. Didn't need any other parts. Film is rolling good now. Nothing else needed.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,15966,06/05/2025,1. Prod Stopped,The compressor quit working on the Large Trimline 1 foam machine.,Closed and Completed,0,2.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/05/2025 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/05/25  7:56:31 AM: Checked voltage to compressor when it should be on. Voltage coming from the board to it is good. Swapped the compressor, wires, tubing, and filters. Cleaned off front jaw. A/B lines were a little too tight when dispenser is at home position. When removing the bracket that holds them, one of the bolts wouldn't break free. Removed mount and took to maintenance. Tried removing bolt but it broke. This has happened before. I just drill out the insert and put a through bolt with lock nut or jam nuts. I will get more brackets and a compressor ordered. Everything else looks good. Turned machine on and let it warm up. Calibrated ejecting with no issues at all. Ran and adjusted recipe as needed. Machine is running good with good foam.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,16505,07/28/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Line stopped up,Closed and Completed,0,6,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/14/2025 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/20/25  4:27:43 AM: Got mixing blocks in. Put a new one on and got recipe adjusted. Didn't have any issues after warming up. Machine is running good with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 08/11/25  5:21:56 AM: There was an issue with our account somehow and parts have yet to arrive. I repaired a mixing block to test. Ran 30-50 molds then it blew up for some reason. Got with Dan 8/8. He is sending some mixing blocks through the warranty. I removed the jaw assembly. Cleaned all inside of the machine after mixing block failure. Removed the dispenser tray assembly. Cleaned and replaced both filters. Cleaned tray and metal filter as well. Removed dispenser solution line and the fitting on the housing. Cleaned both out and put back together. Rebuilt a jaw assembly while awaiting parts. Cleaned all parts. Replaced aluminum rollers. Replaced black knurled rollers. Replaced calendar motor. Replaced all teflon on assembly. Replaced edge seal inserts. Still have one more jaw assembly to clean and rebuild. I need to order parts for that repair so I'll put it on another work order. Hopefully mixing blocks arrive today and I can get this back up and running. | Preston Ellexson - 07/28/25 10:40:21 AM: We don't have anymore mixing blocks. I got more ordered today. I am going to remove and clean what I can today. When mixing blocks arrive, I'll continue this job. I might have to replace the dispenser solution assembly too. Working with Dan to get some more of those ordered as well.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17025,09/17/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large 2 foam machine calender motor,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/17/2025 02:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/17/25 12:31:19 PM: Getting a calendar motor error. Mixing block assembly is really hard to move left and right. Removed film roll and covered ball screw with white lithium grease. Mixing block assembly is moving freely now. Still getting calendar error. Turned machine off and removed the jaw assembly. Cleaned off all foam buildup. It was up to 3/4"" thick on the mixing block side. Cleaned inside machine as well. Put assembly back on and tightened everything. Put film back in and fed through. There was so much foam buildup the mixing block wasn't making it to it's home position. That was causing the calendar error because the mixing block didn't travel far enough to start the mold cycle. Emptied tank and calibrated the eject cycle. Adjusted the recipe and everything is running good now.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17298,10/15/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large trimline 2                Lost power to controller brings machine up and down,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/15/2025 09:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 10/15/25  6:58:33 AM: Removed cover for lift table electrical box underneath. The breaker for it was tripped. Reset breaker and put cover back on. Tested and the lift table is working good. Ran up and down numerous times with no issues. I let Johnny know so he can continue. Jaw assembly needs to be removed and cleaned. Rollers won't move right now. He should be able to clean and get it back operational. I told him to holler if that doesn't get it running. | Preston Ellexson - 10/15/25  5:38:25 AM: Johnny got with me on this. I'll get the lift table functional and he said he'd continue his work after I got that working.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17319,10/16/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large trimline 2 foam machine imold film hanging up,Closed and Completed,0,6,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/16/2025 01:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/16/25 11:57:07 AM: Johnny removed the jaw assembly to clean and still can't get the machine to run. He told me this yesterday. Today I came in and started rebuilding a used jaw assembly. Took it to the machine when I was done. Removed the jaw assembly that was in it and put the rebuilt one in. Put in the mold they were needing. Started machine and it is cutting through the film. Checked and found the film was fed wrong on the back side. It was behind the film sensor and bracket. It is supposed to be in front of it. That was causing the split. Got the film fed back the right way. Ran another and it is putting small little holes in the front film. Removed film roll and found the issue. The front and back film are sticking together from the manufacturers roll. When they separate, it is putting little holes all the way down the film. Removed film roll and put on a new roll. It is not sticking at all on this roll. Got machine started, and after adjusting the recipe a couple times, the foam is looking good. Ran over 60 without any issues, errors, or bad foam. I let Dan know we were having some film issues. He said to save the bad rolls and we can get comped for them. He is going to send that issue up the chain at Sealed Air since we've had 3 or 4 in the past month be no good out of the box. Machine is running good now.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17540,11/03/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Top door falling off hinges,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/04/2025 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 11/05/25  5:51:45 AM: Most of the threads on all 6 hinge bracket holes were pretty worn out. I replaced all hinge bracket bolts with a bolt an inch long. I put a nut on the back side of all 6. Straightened hinge mounts once brackets were tight. Slid door back on the hinges. Tightened the ground wire and the metal flat rod on the door. Turned the machine on and made a quick adjustment to the recipe. Took machine about 20 parts to fully warm up. Made a few more recipe adjustments and machine is running good molds now. No more issues. | Preston Ellexson - 11/04/25  4:05:23 AM: I removed the door hinges and put the door on top of the machine. I need to clean the threads on the machine hinge nuts. I'll put a longer bolt in or bolt and nut them all.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17591,11/06/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large 2 foam machine film is rolling up,Closed and Completed,0,2.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/06/2025 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 11/07/25  8:52:51 AM: Loaded a mold into the machine. Machine wasn't bad, but needed a little cleaning. One of the handles that locks the mold in was broken. I replaced it with new. Had to put a new film roll on. Made adjustments to the recipe before running. First film roll was bad and was tearing during operation. Cleaned mess on machine. I put the bad roll in maintenance for return with a couple others. Tried a new roll in the machine. It was better. Had it happen once, but was fine after that. Got mold running good, then they needed a change out for a different unit. Swapped it all and adjusted recipe as needed. Mold is running good. No more issues with this machine.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,18338,02/02/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",CONTROLLER MOTOR BROKE,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,02/09/2026 08:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 02/09/26  7:40:58 AM: Removed the cover for the calendar motor. Lovejoy coupler was broken on the motor shaft side. Removed the calendar motor with the bracket attached. Removed broken coupler and replaced with new. Tightened set screw and put the motor and bracket back on the machine. Turned the machine on and got it ready. Checked recipe and it looks good. Machine is running good molds with no more issues. | Preston Ellexson - 02/02/26 11:12:56 AM: Got with Johnny on this. It will be Wednesday before I can get to this.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,18820,03/19/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Instamold A chemical barrel on Large Trimline 2 Foam machine has a small puncture on bottom that's causing it to leak. Request to look into a patch option to prevent further spillage.,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Dennis Davis,Maintenance,0,03/19/2026 12:00 PM,"Dennis Davis - 03/19/26 10:23:29 AM: Used some JB weld and a piece of metal to create a patch.
Do not know if it will hold",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,18966,04/02/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Pin broke off,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/03/2026 08:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 04/03/26  6:24:13 AM: They were having a hard time removing the mixing block and accidentally broke the tip of the assembly. I locked the machine out. Removed wiring from mixing block. Removed hose and barb fitting. A line was extremely hard to remove. Just build up over time. Got it off and plugged. Removed B with no issues. Cleaned the fitting on the A line so it would spin somewhat freely. Put new assembly on. Plugged wiring in. Put B line on and tightened. Put A line on and tightened. Put hose back on barb. Double checked everything else on the machine before turning on. Turned on and fed film. Adjusted the recipe. Started running molds. Door pressure was low so I tightened the bolts on the load cell. Molds are running really good now. They don't need any foam right now so I stopped the machine. It is ready to run when they need it.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19055,04/10/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Mixon block stuck on machine,Closed and Completed,0,5,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/21/2026 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/22/26  4:28:36 AM: Removed the lines and power cable from the mixing block assembly. Removed it and the mixing block and replaced with new. Connected A and B lines. Hooked up power cable and dispenser solution tubing. I'm going to rebuild the mixing block I removed. It had very little use on it, and is not built up too bad. Removed lock out tag out and turned machine on to get warming up. There was no film in the machine. Got with Jimmie for a new roll. The adjustable roller bracket that keeps the film tight needed adjusted. I removed it, adjusted the stop plates, and re-installed it. Put film roll in and fed as needed. Adjusted recipe slightly and started machine. Molds started running good once it warmed up. Not too many recipe adjustments were needed. I let Johnny know to order more mixing blocks, and more film rolls. Machine is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 04/14/26 12:14:48 PM: I got the parts in today. I'll get this swapped out tomorrow morning. | Preston Ellexson - 04/10/26 12:28:24 PM: Dan got back with me. He thinks it's the drive assembly that is the issue. Sealed Air changed motors in that assembly and he is not a fan of the new ones. They have been having issues with them. I removed the assembly from the machine, but left everything plugged in. Took top cover off to inspect gears inside. All is good. Nothing is locked up, and there is plenty of grease inside. Removed the ballscrew/motor assembly. The mixing block rod was all the way up in the ballscrew housing. The snap ring on top of the mixing block was twisted and not locked on the rod anymore. I manually pushed it down to remove the bad mixing block. Got the ballscrew to home position. Replaced mixing block with new and put top cover back on. Turned the machine on and tested. No errors on the machine, but it won't shoot A or B chemicals. Tried a couple times with the same result. I'm having Dan send more dispenser assemblies. I'll swap out and go from there when they arrive next week. | Preston Ellexson - 04/10/26  4:37:59 AM: For some reason, the ball screw that operates the mixing block keeps giving us errors. I believe this is a rear console circuit board issue. This happened a few weeks ago. I replaced the mixing block assembly and everything was running good after making machine and recipe adjustments. They called me yesterday with the same issue. Johnny wanted to know if I knew how to remove the mixing block when the assembly was still intact with the top of it. I reached out to Dan at the end of the day yesterday with no response. I am getting with him today after first break. I don't have anymore mixing block assemblies so I locked the machine out and told them to just leave the block as is until I figure it out.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19169,04/22/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large 2 foam machine magnet on door broke,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/22/2026 01:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 04/22/26 11:56:30 AM: Went to the machine to inspect. It looks like the 4 bolts for the door magnet slowly backed out and came unthreaded. The threads on the internal plate were a little messed up. Took to maintenance and ran a tap through to clean. Took back to the machine and put everything back together. I used the old magnet block and the load sensor that was there. They didn't have any damage. Turned the machine on and checked the recipe. Set the door pressure. Started running molds with no issues. Put all covers back on. Machine is running good now. No new parts were needed.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19290,05/05/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Foam Machine door wont close,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/05/2026 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/06/26  6:35:41 AM: Turned machine on and tested. Door works good when running in manual operation. Started molds and after the first few, the door started acting up. We had a new door assembly in maintenance. Turned machine power off and swapped out faulty one with new assembly. Turned power on. Door pressure was high and needed to be lowered. Adjusted the recipe slightly. Started molds and let everything warm up. After warming up ,the door was having issues staying shut. Ran over 40 parts before it started doing this. I lowered the door pressure around 300. When it warms up, the pressure is rising on this machine. Got everything running good with no issues.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19337,05/07/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large 2 foam machine magnet loose on door,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/18/2026 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/18/26  7:18:09 AM: They have the machine running now since film rolls arrived. No issues with function. | Preston Ellexson - 05/12/26  5:13:56 AM: Bolts came loose on the door magnet again. This is the second time it's happened on this machine. I've never had this happen on any machine before. I removed the door panels. Removed the door magnet and parts. Cleaned threads on door magnet plate. Load cell bolts were slightly stripped. Got replacements from maintenance. Put all back together and got the door pressure set. I was going to start running the molds, but they are out of film rolls. Machine is ready to run otherwise.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19637,06/01/2026,2. General Maint - High Priority,motor controller arm not functioning.,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/03/2026 02:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/03/26  4:10:38 AM: Went to the machine. Put in a mold and turned on. Removed the cover for the calendar motor. The lovejoy couplers had a pretty good gap in between each other. Tried feeding film to run. Right edge seal is not reading good. Replaced the inserts in the left and right edge seal. We don't have any more new edge seals w/card. I let Matt know to get a dozen ordered of each. Loosened set screws on both couplers, pushed together, and tightened. Checked recipe and it looks good to start with. Started running parts with no issues. The coupler was the issue. I let the cell know they are ready to run when they need it. I let Matt know as well. | Preston Ellexson - 06/01/26  5:00:07 AM: I am going to look at this after break.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19727,06/05/2026,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",calendar motor,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/05/2026 01:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/05/26 12:27:30 PM: Put a mold in the machine and turned the power on. Edge seals were in very bad shape. We don't have anymore, so I just replaced the inserts with new ones. I realized the teflon aprons weren't installed properly. Replaced 3 that were sliced and put on correctly. Tried running just to see. Calendar motor happens pretty quick. Turned power off. Removed the calendar motor and bracket. Removed the lovejoy coupler from the motor shaft. Removed the motor from the bracket. Put a new motor on and put loctite on the bolts. As I was tightening the set screw on the coupler, the bolt head broke. Took to maintenance and removed the broken bolt. Took back and put on the motor. Got it set to the right depth and put all back on the machine. Turned power on and checked recipe. It looks good to start. The door pressure was too low and needed adjusted. Once it warmed up, the recipe needed slight adjustments. It has ran 60+ molds with no issues. Machine is running good.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19755,06/09/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Calender motor failed,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/11/2026 01:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/17/26  4:28:57 AM: Checked the calendar motor. It doesn't seem loose yet, so I'm wondering why it's having issues. Checked circuit boards for any signs. No issues. Blew out the electrical cabinet. It was full of foam debris and dust. Operator said it isn't cutting very well. I got a code from Dan. Logged in and adjusted the cut wire percentage. Checked the reverse distance as well. Made sure no other settings needed adjusted while I was logged into the special menu. As I was inspecting everything, I realized the right side of the jaw was very wobbly. The bolt that holds the aluminum arm with bearing was broken. Tried removing it with no luck. I have a new and rebuilt jaw assembly in maintenance. Grabbed the rebuilt one and put on the machine. Now it is throwing a cut wire short. I removed the cut wires and threw away the jaw. Got one off of the new assembly in maintenance and put on the machine. Everything is working now. I had to fine tune the recipe, but molds are looking good now. No machine issues right now.",[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,20521,08/27/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Air compressor hot working  large trimline 2,Closed and Completed,0,2,Dennis Davis,Maintenance,0,09/14/2026 12:00 AM,Dennis Davis - 09/16/26  7:10:04 AM: replaced Air compressor.,[]
1944,EQ ID 1944,Large Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,20709,09/15/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Large Trimline 2 boat stripped out on mixing block,Pending,0,0.25,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/21/2026 06:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 09/21/26  4:04:12 AM: Awaiting warranty parts for repair.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1384,05/12/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Need lot of work,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/12/2022 06:45 AM,Preston Ellexson - 05/12/22  6:45:52 AM: Yesterday I welded up the broken brackets up top. Tested the machine but still needs work. This morning I adjusted the sensor aiming down for the mold. Turned machine on and tested. Machine is running good foam.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1517,05/27/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",side A clogged,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/27/2022 11:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/31/22  8:18:44 AM: Removed the mixing block head assembly. Brought to maintenance and took all the way apart to clean. Got all cleaned and back on the machine. The jaw motor coupler was not as tight as it should be. Removed covers and adjusted the motor coupler for a nice tight fit. Put all covers back on and tested machine. It is running good, but did a few with no A or B in bag. Threw a Side B pressure read fail error. Running good now. Not sure what the issue was but will monitor next week.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1719,06/20/2022,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,left edge seal is bad and needs replaced,Closed and Completed,0,0.25,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/20/2022 11:30 AM,Preston Ellexson - 06/20/22  9:59:21 AM: Left edge seal needed replaced. Tested machine and everything is working good.,[]
