1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,1665,06/13/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Nut loose on head,Closed and Completed,0,4,Ronnie @ Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,07/14/2022 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 07/21/22  7:08:59 AM: Ronnie came out and got the issues solved. The ball screw that the mixing block assembly rides on was really dirty. He got it all cleaned and adjusted and machine is running good now. | Preston Ellexson - 06/23/22 10:20:08 AM: *,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,2324,09/06/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Screw strip out,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/09/2022 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/12/22  7:00:13 AM: Got the part in. It is the entire assembly with new wires. Had to put a new mixing block on because it doesn't come with one. The wires were about 10' shorter. Had to splice in an extension to be able to function properly. Got all complete. Put in a mold and tested. After warming up, the foam looks good. Machine is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 09/07/22  4:29:30 AM: The screw that tightens the mixing block is fine, but the threads on the housing are stripped. Called Ronnie and he is going to get the part overnighted if in stock. If it arrives today, I will repair. If it's not here today, I'll get in touch with Ronnie and check the status of the part.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,2354,09/12/2022,1. Prod Stopped,Not reading mode,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston/Ronnie @ Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,09/13/2022 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 09/13/22 10:13:25 AM: Ronnie removed the vacuum motor to see the sensor from the back side. One of the wire leads had fallen off and was dangling. He re-crimped and put all back together. Tested approx. 30 molds with no issues. Machine is good to run. | Preston Ellexson - 09/12/22 11:07:16 AM: Tried different molds with no luck. Checked all settings. It's not reading the molds. Got with Ronnie and he said he thinks it's probably a board on this one. The board on the bottom right that we just ran out of. He will be here tomorrow.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,2445,09/22/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Change out sensor,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/21/2022 01:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 09/23/22  7:41:14 AM: Swapped out the mold sensor while Johnny had the machine apart cleaning.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,2446,09/22/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Foam don't look straight coming down,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/23/2022 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/23/22  7:44:52 AM: Scraped most of the foam build-up off of the machine. Adjusted the film length, the film speed, and the flow. Took a little time to fine tune but machine is running good parts now. Had to adjust the Keyence mold sensor.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,3040,10/25/2022,1. Prod Stopped,Dispenser sulution pressure low,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston/Johnny,Maintenance,0,10/25/2022 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 10/25/22 11:47:19 AM: Mixing block was missing a seal for the dispensing solution. Machine is running good. One of the molds for small trimline isn't reading the file correctly. Sent Ronnie a message and awaiting a response. Other than this, the machine is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 10/25/22 11:11:49 AM: Replaced tubing assembly. Disposed and replaced the dispensing solution. Removed mixing block to check for blockages. Check dispenser solution barb and opening. Cleaned the filter in the dispensing solution container. Tested machine and it is still getting the same error. Got with Ronnie @ Sealed Air and we think it's the compressor. I just used our last one, so I'll have him order more. Shane is ordering more dispensing solution.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,3093,11/01/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",WE'LL NOT PULL IN BAG,Closed and Completed,0,1,Ronnie @ Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,11/11/2022 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 11/23/22  9:47:04 AM: Ronnie came and got the machine going.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,3318,11/21/2022,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,b side high pressure,Closed and Completed,0,6,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/23/2022 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 11/23/22  7:35:41 AM: Removed lines and checked for blockages. A side was stopped up. Replaced filter in fitting. Mixing block is still good. Had to remove the mixing block assembly. It was very hard moving back and forth. Cleaned and sprayed with white lithium grease and it is moving free and easy. Taped up A and B lines where they ride on one of the covers. Had to tape it to make it a smooth transition while moving the mixing block. Cleaned all foam from inside machine. Tested and machine is running ok. Had to mess with the recipe for awhile, but now they are running good.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,3499,12/07/2022,4. Prod Continuing but Affected Equipment stopped,A AND B SIDE HIGH PRESSURE.,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/10/2023 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 01/12/23 10:31:19 AM: Tech support said one of the boards needed replaced. Got Ronnie to order one. Swapped and still getting the issue. Inspected the foam controller motor and found it is slipping when in motion. Had Ronnie send 2. Swapped out and put machine back together. Tested and all is working good with no errors on this issue anymore. | Preston Ellexson - 12/29/22  5:47:29 AM: I've worked on this machine for a week or so off and on. Ronnie came and inspected. Load cell for door might need replaced, but it is working most of the time. We believe there might be a board failing and causing these random issues that are inconsistent. We are now getting an error that won't allow the machine to start-up. I am calling tech support with Ronnie off this week.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,4373,02/14/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Calender motor,Closed and Completed,0,1.25,Preston/Josh,Maintenance,0,02/14/2023 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 02/14/23  9:35:07 AM: Removed and replaced calendar motor. Ran machine. Made adjustments on the recipe until foam looked good. Machine is running good with no issues.,[]
