1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,5117,04/03/2023,1. Prod Stopped,Mold Eject did not P RECHARGE,Closed and Completed,0,5,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/03/2023 12:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/07/23 12:25:10 PM: Replaced 1164FE board and ran about 20 pieces. Now getting a motor communication failure. Replaced the 1164GN board and still same result. Removed the motor assembly for the foam dispenser. Cleaned ball screw and replaced motor with new. Re-assembled everything and still getting same error. Replaced the main 1164GD board and swapped the SD card out. Machine turned on and is running. Had to make many adjustments on the recipe, but after that, machine is running good molds. | Preston Ellexson - 04/03/23 10:33:24 AM: Board is faulty. Compressor pump isn't getting 240V. Awaiting boards to arrive from Sealed Air.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,5560,05/05/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Mold eject,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston/Josh,Maintenance,0,05/08/2023 12:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 05/11/23  8:35:41 AM: Swapped out compressor pump and all is running good.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,5879,06/05/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Getting too much foam,Closed and Completed,0,5,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/06/2023 02:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 06/06/23 12:10:27 PM: Adjusted recipe but kept on getting empty film every 10 or so. It was reading a high b pressure when this happened. Took the mixing block off and replaced all wear parts on it. New mixing blocks should be here 6/8. Getting a low dispenser solution now and realized there was an o-ring missing. Machine is back up and running. Made more adjustments to the recipe and everything is working good right now. I will monitor today and tmrw for any more issues.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,6559,07/21/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Solution is lincoln,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/24/2023 07:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/24/23  5:29:11 AM: Removed mixing block assembly and brought to maintenance. Removed a side valve, cleaned, and replaced all 3 seals. Tightened the allen screw for the housing due to it being loose. B side is fine so I didn't do anything to it. Cleaned all liquids from machine and scraped down any foam build-up. Had to replace a seal in the mixing block as well. Replaced the center foam sensor due to the build-up on it. Cleaned the velcro type pads so they interlock better. Removed the jaw assembly and cleaned. Replaced teflon tape kit but not on the jaw itself by the cut wire. Cleaned cut wire. Warmed up machine and ran. Everything looks good with no issues.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,7155,09/11/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Screen goes blank door wont latch,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/12/2023 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/13/23 12:12:40 PM: Went over Monday. ST-6 mold is having issues. When it starts the mold process, the screen goes blue and everything just stops. No door movement or anything. Got with Ronnie. He suggested main board swap after inspecting wear items for issues. Had to dump the files to USB due to the flash drives being different. Got new one installed and files all loaded. Had a different mold in and everything was working good. Swapped back to the ST-6 mold and still have blue screen issue. This recipe had 4 steps, but can run off of 3 being a small mold. I deleted the 4th step and everything started working fine. There must have been some sort of corrupt file inside the 4th step on the saved file. I adjusted the mold with 3 steps and it has been running since 6/12 @ 8am. All is good. Left the board in since I had to swap all files and recipes.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,7705,10/17/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",A side pressure reading failed,Closed and Completed,0,8,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/17/2023 02:30 PM,Preston Ellexson - 10/31/23 12:17:17 PM: Just got the dispenser assembly replaced. Ran new wires and tied everything up again. Had to replace a few bolts on the mounts. One bolt by the electrical cabinet was broken on the mount bracket. Had to remove the threaded insert and put in a longer bolt/jam nut. Cleaned the entire mixing block and replaced all seals. Ran a few a got a high dispenser solution error. Got with Ronnie for access code. Zeroed solution pressure and adjusted the offset. Ran over 100 now with little to no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 10/24/23  4:04:55 AM: Received in part from Sealed Air to hopefully repair. Will get on this again today.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,8174,11/29/2023,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Running empty bags,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/29/2023 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 12/12/23  7:18:11 AM: Had Patrick change out the mixing block and it has been running good since. | Preston Ellexson - 11/29/23  5:56:27 AM: Checked the recipe and looked at the diagnostics. I adjusted the recipe, but everything else looks good. Last time this happened, the dispenser assembly was swapped out with new. It was the belief that the ball screw operating the dispenser was malfunctioning. I didn't see any blanks for the time I was at the machine, and molds were looking pretty good. Cleaned the foam out of the mold and adjusted recipe again. I will monitor to see if this machine continues to have problems.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,11502,05/03/2024,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",needs general maintenance,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/03/2024 01:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/03/24 11:49:13 AM: Adjusted the recipe and cleaned the teflon tape. Cleaned the cut wire. Still kept having issues. The screen would go blue, door wouldn't shut, and no foam would go. Found a corrupt file on the 3579 recipe. Deleted it from the machine and remade the recipe. Had to adjust many times moving forward. Replaced teflon tape on the jaw. Replaced the the FE board with the one from matte black cell. That machine is down until I get parts Monday. Finally got this making good molds without any issues.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,11874,05/30/2024,"5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",broke the t handle off of the I mold,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/30/2024 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/30/24  5:10:53 AM: Matt came back in maintenance and got with me on this. 2 handles are broken, and we don't have any here right now. We don't have and 5/16-18 couplers either. Welded 2 sets of nuts together. We had some handles with through holts for a 9/16 bolt. I used these for the 5/16 bolts and a jam nut. Put on the machine as tight as I could without unthreading. I am ordering new handles/blocks overnight. Hopefully we'll get them in tomorrow and I can swap out with the original.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,11914,06/03/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped","cant get foam to fully fill the mold, and the door seems to not want to shut fully",Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/03/2024 01:30 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/03/24 11:40:17 AM: Inspected the machine. Found a leak in the tank where it had been rewelded previously. Locked out machine. Removed electrical cover panel on back and removed tank. Took to maintenance, welded it up, and ground down smooth. Put back on machine. Found the electrical box on back was missing the 2 bolts that keep it safely attached. Replaced them so it wouldn't pull off and short out like the PMU one in the past. Got all lines put back on and everything tied in. Turned on and tested. Machine was running ok, but seal wire isn't cutting very well. Removed the back jaw assembly and replaced all teflon tape. Adjusted recipe, cleaned seal wire, and adjusted the door pressure. After fine tuning recipe, everything is running good. No issues since lunch.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,12685,08/07/2024,2. General Maint - High Priority,compressor problems,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/07/2024 10:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/07/24 11:04:21 AM: Compressor is working fine. Bag isn't sucking in when mold starts. Checked voltage to the vacuum motor. Voltage is there, but motor isn't working. Swapped with new and everything is working good now. Adjusted the recipe and machine is running good molds. Checked the vacuum motor I pulled off, and one of the motor brushes is pretty much done. I am getting with Ronnie to see if they sell replacement brushes.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,13698,11/06/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",A Side pressure reading failed,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,11/11/2024 10:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 11/25/24  7:21:22 AM: Replaced entire dispenser assembly. I believe the motor/ball screw was faulty on the old one causing a high pressure reading. Got swapped out and adjusted recipe. Machine is running good.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,14146,12/18/2024,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door won't close on foam machine,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,12/18/2024 09:00 AM,Preston Ellexson - 02/11/25  5:56:09 AM: Got this fixed awhile back. Adjusted door pressure and made some recipe adjustments. Everything is running good.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,14402,01/20/2025,1. Prod Stopped,Door won't close screen goes blank,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston/Dennis,Maintenance,0,01/22/2025 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 01/28/25  5:51:53 AM: Changed molds and everything runs with no problem. Loaded the other mold back in and tested. Still getting blanks, no door movement and screen goes blue or black. Removed mold and cycled machine power. Took a flash drive to the large trimline 2 IMold and copied all of the recipes. Went back to small trimline and deleted all recipes from the memory card. Loaded the flash drive recipes on one by one. Put mold in and everything is working. Had to adjust the recipe and checked all wear items on machine. Replaced some teflon on the jaw. Machine is running good.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,14538,01/31/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Corner foam mode needs repair,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/31/2025 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 02/05/25  6:23:56 AM: Took apart 2 molds. Cleaned both. Removed broken screws. Replaced all screws with new. Checked for gapping and everything looks good. Both molds were put back together and are ready for use.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,14810,02/25/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",B side drum is empty     is not empty drum is full,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston/Dan@Sealed Air,Maintenance,0,03/04/2025 12:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 03/05/25  5:55:10 AM: B motor/pump isn't running. Removed the cover on the rear console. Found a capacitor that had blown. Replaced the main board on the rear console. Got all covers back on and turned machine on. Got a low current error on B side motor/pump. Swapped out the brushes with new. Now it's not shooting any A or B. Got with Dan @ Sealed Air and he said you have to re-program the rear board when replaced. They have 1 program key so he had to come out. Got it all set to the right parameters. Ran machine and everything is working good now. Adjusted the recipe and molds are looking good.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,15323,04/08/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Losing air,Closed and Completed,0,2.5,Preston,Maintenance,0,04/08/2025 02:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 04/09/25  4:40:22 AM: Molds were blowing out a little inside while curing. I adjusted the recipe a little bit, but still acting up every few parts. Had to clean a few times due to the door closing and getting fresh components on mold and door so it was very sticky. Unplugged and removed the vacuum motor. The seal on the valve eject was completely loose and was moving up and down as the eject valve was initiated. We have no more new ones in maintenance. Dug through the old ones and got one that still had good edges around the top of the seal. Super glued back down in place. Let it dry and put it on the machine. Emptied tank pressure and ran eject cycle. Machine is running much better now. No issues with the film not pulling in any more. Also put on a rebuilt jaw with new teflon and a new top wire. Rebuilt the one that was on it and it is in maintenance ready to use. Ran 50+ molds with no issues. Removed door motor cover and sprayed gears with lithium grease. They were noisy when in operation. Machine is running good.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,15843,05/21/2025,1. Prod Stopped,Running empty binag,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/06/2025 07:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/06/25  8:33:09 AM: Got the dispenser assembly in. Swapped it out. Ran the new cable and harness to the rear console board. Swapped one teflon apron. Cleaned front jaw teflon. Swapped out the dispenser solution tubing assembly. Turned machine on and tested. It is putting in dispenser solution but still no A/B mixture still. Turned back off. Replaced the FE circuit board in the back. Replaced the mixing block with a new one. Turned  machine on. Emptied air from rear tank. Calibrated eject cycle. Started running and it's finally working. Had to adjust recipe for a bit but foam is running good now. | Preston Ellexson - 06/02/25  7:58:29 AM: Wrong part was delivered. Got with Dan to get the right one sent. | Preston Ellexson - 05/23/25 11:38:33 AM: Dan got parts ordered today. Machine is locked out. When I return the week after, I'll get right back on this with new parts. | Preston Ellexson - 05/22/25 12:06:17 PM: Removed mixing block. Replaced all filters and o-rings. Slightly opened the A and B valves individually with the mixing block off. They are flowing with nothing stopped up. Put all back together and ran mold cycle. Still just dispenser solution but no A and B. Getting high side A pressure but not B. Fairly certain I need to change the dispenser solution assembly. We are out so I had to get with Dan @ Sealed Air and he ordered 2 for us. I will change this out when it arrives and go from there.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,16081,06/16/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Film keep hanging up,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/16/2025 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 06/23/25  7:38:28 AM: They had a film break that caused a/b mixture to make a big mess inside the machine. Cleaned everything off. Replaced the front film sensor due to foam damage. Replaced the mold block sensor due to foam damage as well. I had an entire rebuilt jaw assembly in maintenance. I put it on due to the mess with the other one. I think it was just a recipe issue and the cut wires. After I got all the parts swapped out I started running molds. Ran 25-30 and had one issue. Had to clean a little bit up, but no replacements of anything. Continued running with a recipe adjustment. Ran over 60 without any issues. Machine is running good.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,16236,06/26/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Mold box sensor messed up,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,06/27/2025 01:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 07/02/25  5:00:01 AM: Cleaned up mess. Removed entire jaw assembly. Cleaned and adjusted sensors after a leak occurred. Replaced the left side apron velcro strip on the bracket. Cleaned jaw assembly where needed. Put all back together and turned machine on. Tested everything with no issues. Started running mold. Made adjustments to the recipe and everything is now running good.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,16523,07/29/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Bag rolling up in the machine,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,08/01/2025 12:00 PM,"Preston Ellexson - 08/08/25  4:29:26 AM: Ended up needing a new compressor. Board is sending out voltage the way it should. Got compressor swapped out. Started machine up. Once it started running, I didn't have any issues with the operation. Made recipe adjustments. No roller issues or back rolling the film. Not sure why this was happening before. I ran over 50 without any issues. Machine is good to run. | Preston Ellexson - 07/29/25 12:26:30 PM: Went over to machine. Tried to run one and it seems to be a roller or bearing going bad. When I ran it, it gave a precharge didn't meet pressure error. Ran eject cycle and the compressor isn't even kicking on. I will go over first thing and see if it's a board or compressor issue. I am in the middle of rebuilding an entire jaw assembly already. I will likely need to complete this repair so I can use it on the machine. I'm adding my time for the jaw assembly to this work order.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,16839,08/27/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",NO air pressure,Closed and Completed,0,1.5,Preston/Johnny,Maintenance,0,09/15/2025 07:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/15/25  5:26:22 AM: Johnny got the jaw assembly swapped out. He is having air pressure issues still. I swapped out the bloffer and everything is working good now. Molds look good. | Preston Ellexson - 08/28/25  4:25:07 AM: Johnny was having an issue with the machine building pressure. He tried 2 different bloffers with no change. He turned the power off. I went over after lunch and turned on. It won't even roll the film down straight for me. Left and right side are not feeding down, but back up into the machine. Nothing is locked up. This is a fairly new entire jaw assembly. Had him come out for a second set of eyes, and he doesn't see anything wrong either aside from function. Got with Dan to send another jaw assembly. It'll either be here 8/29 or next week. I'll swap it when it arrives and go from there.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17084,09/29/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Mold sensor,Closed and Completed,0,0.75,Preston,Maintenance,0,09/29/2025 10:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 09/29/25  8:36:39 AM: Machine was getting calendar motor error and mold box not clear error. Unplugged harnesses, removed teflon apron strips, and removed jaw assembly. Cleaned and adjusted sensor to where it should be good. Cleaned buildup from teflon apron strips. Removed cover for calendar motor. Couplers had a good gap between them but nothing is broken and motor is still good. Adjusted both love joy couplers tight together and tightened set screws. Put jaw assembly back on. Put on teflon apron strips and metal plate. Plugged everything back in and turned machine on. Had to fine tune the adjustment on the mold box sensor. Adjusted recipe and started running. Took 10+ parts to warm up. Everything is working good with no errors. Molds are looking good and running smooth.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,17476,10/27/2025,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",B side stop up,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,10/27/2025 02:00 PM,Preston Ellexson - 10/28/25  7:15:52 AM: I put a mold block in the machine and powered up. Machine is getting a b side pump motor current error. Turned power off and checked the motor brushes on b side pump. They are still good size and in good shape. Put back in place and made sure they seated well. Turned machine back on and everything is working good with no errors. Had to let the machine warm up due to sitting for days. Got the recipe adjusted slightly and molds are looking good. Machine is running good with no errors.,[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,18251,01/20/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Bored gone out,Closed and Completed,0,2,Preston,Maintenance,0,01/21/2026 08:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 02/02/26  4:11:06 AM: Johnny let me know that the front sensor wasn't coming on at all. I removed the jaw assembly. Replaced the front film sensor and adjusted as needed. It had been accidentally cut by a knife. Put the jaw assembly back on. Turned machine on to test. Film sensor was coming on, but not working properly. Removed jaw assembly again and replaced this sensor as well. Got it adjusted. Turned machine back on to test. Calendar motor really needs to be replaced. Once it started the motor works fine. You have to hold it tight in position while film feeding the first time. Got it started and everything is running good. Molds look good. I will replace the calendar motor as soon as I get a little free time.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,18439,02/11/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Black roller hanging up,Closed and Completed,0,6,Preston,Maintenance,0,03/17/2026 10:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 03/17/26  7:48:57 AM: Got parts in. I replaced the door assembly with a new one. Unlocked machine and tested. Vacuum motor isn't turning on. Replaced vacuum motor with a new one. Machine is running now. Made a few adjustments to the recipe while running parts to test. Ran over 40 parts with no issues. Recipe is making good molds. Machine is running good. | Preston Ellexson - 03/09/26 11:31:32 AM: I got a new jaw assembly ordered and delivered last week during my PTO. I removed the jaw assembly on the machine and replaced with the new one. Vacuum motor was missing. Got with Johnny and he gave me 2 used ones. He believes one is no good. Put one on the machine. Started machine up and got it ready with a mold and mold block. Tested door with no issues. Tested vacuum with no issues. Calibrated the eject with no issues. Adjusted recipe slightly. Started machine and ran 5-10 pieces. Door stopped shutting after that. When I hit the button to close the door, it only goes a few degrees then stops. I can hit the button continuously and it works. When I go to run a mold now, the vacuum doesn't engage at all. Checked voltage coming out of the board and it is good. I am trying another used vacuum motor just to see. Got with Dan@Sealed Air. He is sending a door assembly, vacuum motors, and more bloffers. If the other vacuum motor doesn't fix it, I'll have to wait until parts arrive to proceed repairing. | Preston Ellexson - 02/16/26 12:13:30 PM: I have a jaw assembly in maintenance that just needs a new film motor. I will get this done tomorrow and hopefully just swap out the jaw assembly with the faulty one.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19237,04/28/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Small trimline foam machine how in air tank,Closed and Completed,0,4,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/04/2026 10:30 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 05/04/26  8:51:14 AM: Turned the machine on to check. Tank is leaking. Had one in maintenance that needed repaired. Got it welded up and smoothed down. Took to the machine. Got covers removed and leaking tank removed. Put repaired tank on machine. Swapped out air fittings and tightened everything. Turned machine on and checked everything. Door pressure wouldn't go up much higher than 300. Removed needed covers and replaced the door load cell. Set door pressure as needed. Replaced the jaw on it. Teflon was really bad and causing issues when running. Made slight adjustments to the recipe. After warming up, the molds are looking good now. I welded up the tank I removed and have it in maintenance for backup. I replaced the teflon on the jaw for backup as well.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,19996,06/30/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",Door wont Clothes are Open,Closed and Completed,0,3,Preston,Maintenance,0,07/09/2026 09:00 AM,"Preston Ellexson - 07/09/26  6:57:22 AM: Got a new door assembly in yesterday. Swapped it out with the old one. This fixed the door issue. Once I got the mold and machine warmed up, it started having cutting issues. This was causing some spills inside and the door was sticking shut. I removed the teflon assembly. Cleaned all old teflon off and cleaned residual glue with acetone. Replaced all teflon  strips. Replaced the apron strips too. Swapped out the jaw with a new one. The bottom wire was starting to show through the teflon. Got all back on the machine. After warming up, I made slight adjustments to the recipe and molds are running good. | Preston Ellexson - 07/01/26  4:15:13 AM: I'll look at this today and figure out what we need to order/repair to get this up and running.",[]
1968,EQ ID 1968,Small Trimline Foam Machine,Assembly,20642,09/09/2026,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",B Side pump low current,Closed and Completed,0,0.5,Dennis Davis,Maintenance,0,09/10/2026 01:30 PM,Dennis Davis - 09/11/26  9:53:59 AM: Replaced brushes on B side motor,[]
1979,EQ ID 1979,PMU Rivet Gun #10,Assembly,1437,05/20/2022,"3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",WON'T PULL RIVET,Closed and Completed,0,1,Preston,Maintenance,0,05/20/2022 10:15 AM,Preston Ellexson - 05/20/22  8:31:37 AM: Disassembled the gun completely. The head had to be pried off the body due to wear. The threads on the rivet gun head were bad. Ordered a tap and cleaned threads up. Put gun back together. Tested and gun is working really good. Sent back to Alex in PMU2.,[]
